  <div class="tip warn">
    <b>Level Suppression:</b> when your Godsworn is below the monster's level, you <b>take more damage and deal less</b> — and the bigger the gap, the worse it gets. Don't push a chapter ahead of your level: go back, raise your cap, and return. Pushing through is slower than backing off.
  </div>

  <p>The <b>Echo of the Boss</b> lets you challenge the boss again — and since the boss is a guaranteed Set-piece source, Echoes are your resource for "farming the piece I'm missing."</p>
</section>

<section id="city">
  <h2 class="serif"><span class="num">17</span>The city</h2>
  <p class="sub">Long-term power doesn't come from loot — it comes from here.</p>

  <div class="grid g2">
    <div class="card"><h4>Temple</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Blessing and Baptism. Each Blessing has a <b>4% chance to grant 1 Talent point</b>. Blessing level tops out at 50 with the building maxed.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>Workshop</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Forging and socketing. Its level sets the Forging cap and lowers prices.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>Stele</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Stage quests, the <b>Awareness</b> cap, and the <b>Preferred Skills</b> cap. Completing stages early unlocks bigger upgrades on the other buildings.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>Prison</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Where Godsworn are born. Its Renovations unlock the high rarities — see section 07.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>Market</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Buy, sell, and <b>Orders</b> (turn in a specific piece, get rare resources). Also has the Vault, which lists high-quality gear for Runes.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>Sanctuary</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Special combinations, like Faith Skulls into Crystallized Skulls.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>Warehouse</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Extended storage and the <b>Vault</b>: a separate high-quality store with stacking. Keeps your bag from clogging up.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>Golem</h4><p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem">Attribute bonuses that apply to <b>every Godsworn of that class</b> — account-wide progression. The cap rises with your Worshiper level.</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="tip">
    <b>Inspire</b> grants a Godsworn a Mastery <b>from another class</b>. The amount and cap rise with upgrades — it's the main source of hybrid builds, alongside Runewords.
  </div>
</section>

<section id="pro">
  <h2 class="serif"><span class="num">18</span>How to get good</h2>
  <p class="sub">A summary of what actually moves the needle, in order of impact.</p>

  <ol class="ladder">
    <li><b>Respect casting priority</b>Support &gt; Utility &gt; Mastery &gt; Basic. If your Mastery isn't firing, you have too many high-priority skills. Cause #1 of a build with no damage.</li>
    <li><b>Buy the Prison's rarity Renovations</b>Without them, Rare-or-better prisoners <b>don't exist</b>. After that, use Warp to manufacture a good Godsworn instead of waiting for one.</li>
    <li><b>Fit in a Sunder source</b>Five stacks = −50% target defense. The cheapest multiplier in the game.</li>
    <li><b>Concentrate on your advance team</b>Opening a chapter raises the level cap for all nine Godsworn. Spreading gear across three average teams stalls everyone.</li>
    <li><b>Chase the set, not the rarity</b>Four Green pieces that turn on a trigger beat four loose Mythics.</li>
    <li><b>Raise the Divine Tower early</b>Permanent, compounding bonus.</li>
    <li><b>Refine before socketing</b>A socketed item can no longer be Refined.</li>
    <li><b>Don't play ahead of your level</b>Level Suppression punishes both ways.</li>
    <li><b>Pick your Basic for its effect</b>It exists to generate Mettle, Haste, or Sunder — not to deal damage.</li>
    <li><b>Mark Preferred Skills before recruiting</b>Deciding the build first is what makes the Prison work for you.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

